cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DDONGGAE: an autonomous polyhedron-collecting robot"
message: If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
abstract: >-
  DDONGGAE (똥개, "DNN-based Detection of Objects with Navigation and
  Goal-oriented Grasping for Autonomous Errands") is a ROS 2 Humble
  autonomous mobile manipulator that searches a
  4 m x 4 m arena, recognises printed-face polyhedral objects with a two-stage
  YOLO segmentation pipeline trained entirely on Blender-synthesised data, drives
  to them without Nav2 using known-map LiDAR localisation, grasps them and
  deposits them in a storage bin within three-minute rounds. First place out of
  16 teams at the SNU AI ROBOT CHALLENGE 2026.
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/YenCho/ddonggae
keywords:
  - robotics
  - ROS 2
  - mecanum drive
  - instance segmentation
  - synthetic data
  - sim-to-real
  - Isaac Sim
  - autonomous manipulation

